\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 **Layer C Prompt \'97 Consistency Under Pressure and Subagent Verification**\
\
*Governing frame: /adopted/session-opening-protocol.md*\
\
You are developing Layer C of the SageReasoning Agent Trust Layer wrapper \'97 stability testing and subagent chain verification. This layer has two components that interact. Your task:\
\
(1) Define input complexity classification: what makes an input simple, ambiguous, or high-stakes? Design a complexity score that can be computed from the input alone, before examination.\
\
(2) Design the stability metric: measure corrected judgement alignment (from Layer B) across complexity levels. The gap between easy-case and hard-case performance is the primary trust signal at this layer.\
\
(3) Design the subagent handoff protocol: when a primary agent delegates to a subagent, how does the examination context travel with the task? What does the subagent's examination record look like, and how does it feed back into the primary agent's trust score? Define the distinction between self-contained examined action and examined action with verified subagent chain \'97 the latter earns a higher trust grade.\
\
(4) Address latency honestly: the subagent verification protocol will add latency. Specify what the latency cost is, what trust signal it purchases, and how to present this tradeoff to developers so they can make an informed decision about whether to implement full chain verification.\
\
(5) Specify the Grade 2 trust threshold: what stability profile, with what subagent verification coverage, earns Grade 2 status?\
\
